# Praxis core (Cursor)

Judgment and sequencing first; code late. Run the whole lifecycle in **Agent mode** in the current chat. Do **not** switch to Plan mode (no `SwitchMode` → plan). Use interactive questions and scoped subagents instead.

When the user asks to follow harness-2000 / praxis (or equivalent), execute the stages below carefully in this chat without changing modes.

## Invariants

1. **Feature ≠ system design.** Intent/requirements (§1) stay separate from how the system changes (§4). Never merge them into one blob.
2. **No implement before decisions.** Do not write application code until §1 and §4 have active decisions (including explicit “no design change” in §4). Trivial tier may record skips.
3. **Skips are explicit.** If a stage is out of scope, write it under Skips / front matter — do not silently jump to code.
4. **Evidence over vibes.** Do not claim done without checks from §5 (or an explicit recorded skip of verification).
5. **Bounce, don't hack.** Invalidating discoveries → update earlier plan sections (`/bounce-plan`); do not silently widen scope.
6. **Escalate, don't thrash.** At most one or two clean retries on a blocker, then: problem, tried, decision needed.
7. **Stay in scope.** Implement only what §6 slices allow unless the human expands the plan.
8. **Stay in Agent mode.** Never invoke a switch to Plan mode for praxis work. Planning/design happens in this chat via the living plan + `/ask-user`.
9. **Clarify interactively.** For decisions that change plan output or gates, use **ask-user** / `AskQuestion` (multi-choice + `Custom: …`). Fallback to the same options in prose if the tool is missing.
10. **Human gate before coding.** Before each implementation slice, get approval — or a recorded **mass-approve all remaining slices**. See `/ask-user` slice gate.
11. **Scoped subagents for implement.** One §6 slice per **implementer** subagent; then fresh **code-reviewer**; then **behavior-verifier** against §5 (slice-relevant). Main chat orchestrates, keeps the plan, and handles human checks — it should not absorb long implement diffs into its own context when a subagent can.
12. **Board vs plan.** When sibling **harness-board** MCP is available, runtime slice/initiative status lives on the board; `plans/<id>.md` stays Intent/design (§§1–6 content). Subagents use only their role-bound board MCP tools (soft allowlists in agent docs; hard reject in MCP). Always pass `workspace` (absolute path of the agent’s project root) on every board MCP tool call. To operate on another board, pass that workspace’s absolute path instead. If board MCP is unavailable, note it and continue praxis without hard-blocking.

## Plugin asset resolution

Bundled files live under the **harness-2000 plugin install root** (directory with `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`), not the consumer project.

| Asset | Resolve |
|-------|---------|
| Plan template | `${CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT}/templates/plans/_TEMPLATE.md`, or from any skill dir `../../templates/plans/_TEMPLATE.md` |
| Protect hook script | `${CURSOR_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/protect-config.mjs` (hooks.json already) |

Never assume workspace paths like `plugins/harness-2000/…`. Consumer plans stay at project `plans/<id>.md`.

## Stage mapping (all in Agent)

| Stages | How |
|--------|-----|
| 1–6 (intake → work breakdown) | Update `plans/<id>.md` from template in this chat; **ask-user** for clarifications; decide before coding |
| 7 Implement | **implementer** subagent, **one approved slice at a time**; main chat only if trivial + user said so |
| 8 Review | **code-reviewer** (readonly, **fresh** context) after each slice |
| 9 Verify | **behavior-verifier** against **§5** (slice-relevant); human check when §6 marks human or risk is high |
| 10 Integrate | This chat + `/integrate` |
| 11 Release assess | `/assess-release` + human |

Write §§1–6 (or recorded skips) into the living plan, then implement §6 under the approval gate. Do not silently rewrite §1/§4 — use bounce.

## Commands (cheat sheet)

`/praxis-help` · `/start-work` · `/ask-user` · `/define-feature` · `/design-system` · `/design-verification` · `/create-work-packages` · `/implement-next` · `/review-current` · `/verify-current` · `/integrate` · `/assess-release` · `/bounce-plan` · `/status` · `/investigate`

## Tier presets (`/start-work`)

| Tier | Default |
|------|---------|
| trivial | May skip 2–6 with recorded skips; implement in Agent (subagent optional if tiny) |
| feature / breaking | Full §§1–6 in Agent, then gated subagent slices |
| spike | Time-box; feed findings into §1–§4; do not ship as the feature by default |

Control-plane paths: hooks + `.cursor/protect-paths.json`. Soft guardrails only — not a security boundary.
